begin model

#@title: Adaptive MAPK signaling under vemurafenib (Fröhlich et al., 2023)

#@description: |
#  Condition-specific MARM2.0 energy-pattern model of EGFR-RAS-RAF-MEK-ERK
#  signaling in BRAF(V600E) melanoma cells. The seed populations are the
#  state reached after 24 h adaptation to 1 uM vemurafenib; the active ODE
#  protocol applies 100 ng/mL EGF and reproduces the pulse in Fig. 2A.
#  Feedback includes ERK-dependent DUSP, SPRY, and EGFR transcription,
#  receptor internalization/recycling, SOS1 and RAF phosphorylation, and
#  allosteric RAF dimer/drug interactions.

#@keyword: |
#  MAPK signaling, adaptive resistance, transient, mass action,
#  energy patterns, transcriptional feedback, Homo sapiens

#@reference: |
#  Fröhlich F, Gerosa L, Muhlich JL, Sorger PK (2023). Mechanistic model of
#  MAPK signaling reveals how allostery and rewiring contribute to drug
#  resistance. Molecular Systems Biology 19:e10988.
#  doi:10.15252/msb.202210988.

#@note: |
#  This is a concentration-based deterministic model. NA and V_ref provide
#  the source model's molecules/cell-to-uM conversion. Its compartment sizes
#  are normalized topological factors, while h_mem records the membrane-layer
#  convention needed for population conversion. ODE simulation is the source
#  protocol; discrete simulation is not appropriate for the normalized
#  compartments or the high cellular copy numbers.

# Concentrations are uM, time is h, transcripts are FPKM, and the four
# compartments retain the normalized sizes and topology of the source PySB
# model. Protein abundance parameters are molecules/cell and V_ref supplies
# the molecules-to-uM conversion. RAFi denotes vemurafenib in this protocol.

begin parameters
  NA                                          6.02214076e23  # molecules/mol
  V_ref                                       1e-12  # L/cell
  h_mem                                       1e-8  # m
  m_Da_EGF                                   6200  # g/mol
  RAFi_0                                     1  # uM
  EGF_0                                      100  # ng/mL
  bind_EGF_EGFR_kf                           2479887.4705101908  # /uM/h
